face-image: img/events/pit_rally.jpg

= The Pit Deputies

NACODS, the union of the pit deputies who certify that a mine is safe to work, has voted to strike against the closure plan. Without them, even the working pits in Nottinghamshire would have to shut.

- @settle_nacods: Settle with the pit deputies.
- @face_nacods: Let the Coal Board face them down.

@settle_nacods
subtitle: -0.5 budget. The working pits stay open.
on-arrival: budget -= 0.5; strike_strength -= 4; dry_dissent += 2

The Coal Board agrees a new review procedure for closures. The deputies call off their strike, and the NUM is left on its own.

@face_nacods
subtitle: A gamble: it may break the strike, or win it for the miners.
on-arrival: {!
Q.nacods_struck = (Math.random() < 0.4) ? 1 : 0;
if (Q.nacods_struck) {
    Q.strike_strength += 20;
    Q.thatcher_rating -= 3;
} else {
    Q.strike_strength -= 6;
}
!}

[? if nacods_struck = 1 : The deputies walk out. The working pits close for a fortnight, and the coal reaching the power stations slows to a trickle. ?][? if nacods_struck = 0 : The deputies back down at the last minute. The working pits stay open. ?]

