on-arrival: miners_strike = 3; union_power += 15; num_mood = 55; thatcher_rating -= 10; rebellion += 3; budget -= 2; economic_growth -= 1; c2_con -= 2; dry_dissent += 10; strike_wave += 2
face-image: img/events/pit_rally.jpg

= The Lights Go Out

The coal stocks at the power stations have run out. The Central Electricity Generating Board starts rota cuts, and for the first time since 1974 the lights go out across Britain. The government settles on the miners' terms. The closures are abandoned, and [+ num_leader +] tells a rally that the miners have beaten two Tory governments.

@negotiated_end
title: A Settlement
tags: event
view-if: con_in_government = 1 and miners_strike = 1 and strike_months >= 13 and strike_strength >= 50
max-visits: 1
new-page: true
on-arrival: miners_strike = 4; union_power += 5; num_mood -= 10; thatcher_rating -= 2; dry_dissent += 6; strike_wave = 1
face-image: img/events/pit_rally.jpg

= A Settlement

After more than a year, ACAS brokers a deal. The closure programme will go ahead more slowly, with an independent review for each pit. Both sides claim victory, and neither believes it.
